{"uid":"e1114b3988be94ba","name":"test_amend_repoint_moves_an_orphaned_ruling_onto_a_live_task_with_no_hand_edit","fullName":"tests.test_operator_ruling#test_amend_repoint_moves_an_orphaned_ruling_onto_a_live_task_with_no_hand_edit","historyId":"3db09344a79f79c8e08142a5d9be4455","time":{"start":1791945876755,"stop":1791945877600,"duration":845},"description":"`ralphctl amend --repoint SEQ --to <task-id>` is the D.11-escalated\n    orphaning's one-command fix: no hand-edit of the amendment file under\n    `config_root/amendments/` -- the CLI rewrites the header's `task:`\n    line and renames the file in place (`engine.state.repoint_amendment`),\n    so the same SEQ number now round-trips as bound to the new, live\n    task id, both in the file on disk and through `amend --list`.","descriptionHtml":"<p><code>ralphctl amend --repoint SEQ --to &lt;task-id&gt;</code> is the D.11-escalated<br />\norphaning's one-command fix: no hand-edit of the amendment file under<br />\n<code>config_root/amendments/</code> -- the CLI rewrites the header's <code>task:</code><br />\nline and renames the file in place (<code>engine.state.repoint_amendment</code>),<br />\nso the same SEQ number now round-trips as bound to the new, live<br />\ntask id, both in the file on disk and through <code>amend --list</code>.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791945777623,"stop":1791945777623,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791945777623,"stop":1791945777623,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"